Add the vivid seed-chroma generator next to `generateColorSchemeFromSeed` (after line 181). It must live in this file to reuse the private `toComposeColorScheme()` (693), `shouldUseNeutralArtworkScheme` (616) and `toGrayscaleColorScheme` (632).

```kotlin
/** App-wide accent (Settings › Appearance › Accent Color): TonalSpot roles/surfaces, primary palette at the seed's own chroma (min 36). Owner option A "vivid", same maths as iOS SchemeBuilder.accentPair. */
fun generateAccentColorSchemePair(seedArgb: Int): ColorSchemePair = runCatching {
    val source = Hct.fromInt(seedArgb)
    fun scheme(isDark: Boolean): ColorScheme {
        val base = SchemeTonalSpot(source, isDark, 0.0)
        return DynamicScheme(source, Variant.TONAL_SPOT, isDark, 0.0,
            TonalPalette.fromHueAndChroma(source.hue, max(36.0, source.chroma)),
            base.secondaryPalette, base.tertiaryPalette, base.neutralPalette, base.neutralVariantPalette
        ).toComposeColorScheme()
    }
    val pair = ColorSchemePair(scheme(false), scheme(true))
    if (shouldUseNeutralArtworkScheme(seedArgb, source)) ColorSchemePair(pair.light.toGrayscaleColorScheme(), pair.dark.toGrayscaleColorScheme()) else pair
}.getOrElse { ColorSchemePair(LightColorScheme, DarkColorScheme) }
```

Imports to add: `com.google.android.material.color.utilities.TonalPalette` and `.Variant`.

Also add `object AccentColorSchemes { fun pairFor(seedArgb: Int): ColorSchemePair }`:
- It memoises results in a `java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap<Int, ColorSchemePair>`, cleared once it holds more than 24 entries.
- Do not use `android.util.LruCache`, which is a stub in JVM unit tests.
- Memoising matters because `ColorScheme` has no `equals`: the same seed must return the same instance, or `remember` / `distinctUntilChanged` keys will recompose the whole app.
- The function is never called on the main thread (cost in risks).

